Let an embedder tell a daemon a level other than its own gate.

RemoteStore::setOptions sends nix::verbosity to the daemon at
handshake, and the daemon logs at that level. The client re-raises each
daemon line with printError, so the line loses its level and reaches
stderr as an error.

An embedder such as huggorm pins nix::verbosity once, before any Nix
thread exists, because printMsg reads it on every thread and a later
write is a data race. A pin at CHATTY then asks every daemon to log at
CHATTY, and libstore's CHATTY sites in GC, substitution and the
builders reach an unsubscribed caller's stderr as errors.

remoteVerbosity is the level setOptions sends. It is atomic, so the
embedder can move it while other threads open connections. Below zero,
the default, setOptions sends nix::verbosity as before, so `nix` and
every other caller see no change.

